Z||000000||bHooper||04-26-2001||03:43 PM||||what is the diffence between the auto tranny's that were used on the 2.8?  i have been discusing this with Doug.  he just got a '86 GT with the "GX-3 auto tranny, with it's 3.33 final drive, and i am buying his '86 SE (there, the rabbit is out of the hat on that one), that has a 3.64 final drive.<P>what diffence will/would i notice?  i have only drivin one auto fiero, Bob Englert's '87 GT (and he thinks that car has a shift kit and 3.1 engine).  <P>will it be as quick, from takeoff... but with a little less wind int he sails at high speed?<P>thanks a bunch!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's<BR>and spellcheck crash's windows<BR>Poly Bushings<BR>Accel Coil||||reg||5
Z||000001||KEV||04-26-2001||04:42 PM|||| WELL FROM WHAT I REMEBER READING THE V6 AUTO'S IN 85&86 RAN THE 3.06 TRANS AND THE 87&88 RAN THE 3.33. THE FOUR CYL USED THE 3.18 TRANS FROM 84 TO 86 AND IN 87 TO 88 WENT TO THE 2.64 TRANS GEARING. I HOPE THIS HELPS.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ray b||04-26-2001||09:15 PM|||| my 88 was a 4 and fealt slow with v-6 swaped in but with stock 4 cly tran at 2.6<BR>mini van tran has 3.6 anyone know the code for it?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||04-26-2001||09:50 PM||||The 85 and 86 V6 autos have a 3.65 final<BR>drive and the 87-88's have a 3.33.<BR>I have driven both and there is not much of a<BR>difference. Obviously the lower geared ones<BR>are a little quicker off the line (barely) and the higher (by higher i mean 3.33) rev's<BR>a little lower at higher speeds. Note: this is a very SMALL difference, about 200 RPMs.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||04-26-2001||10:25 PM||||thanks, dave... that was the kind of answer i was looking for.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>so, it sounds like that GT tranny (the 3.33) is a little "sportier", and the one used in the SE's (and 4 banger's) is probably going to be better for a daily driver/commuter sort of thing?!<P>that would work out great, as i'm hoping to use this car as a daily driver/commuter, for 6 months or a year.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000005||BC-GT||04-26-2001||10:40 PM||||Gear ratios for manual transaxles<BR>                                          Final <BR>         1st    2nd    3rd    4th   5th   Drive  RPO<BR>1984 L4  3.53   1.95   1.24   0.73        3.32   MY8<BR>1984 L4  3.53   1.95   1.24   0.73        4.10   M19<BR>1985 L4  3.73   2.04   1.45   1.03  0.74  3.35   MT2<BR>1985 V6  3.31   1.95   1.24   0.81        3.65   M17<BR>1986 L4  3.73   2.04   1.45   1.03  0.74  3.35   MT2<BR>1986 V6  3.31   1.95   1.24   0.81        3.65   M17<BR>1987 L4  3.73   2.04   1.45   1.03  0.74  3.35   MT2<BR>1987 V6  3.50   2.05   1.38   0.94  0.72  3.61   MG2<BR>1988 L4  3.73   2.04   1.45   1.03  0.74  3.35   MT2<BR>1988 V6  3.50   2.05   1.38   0.94  0.72  3.61   MG2<P>Gear ratios for automatic transaxles<BR>         1st     2nd    3rd<BR>MD9      2.84   1.60    1.00<P>       Final<BR>       Drive   Code   RPO<BR>1984   3.18    PF     MD9<BR>1985   3.06    CD     MD9<BR>1985   3.18    PF     MD9<BR>1986   3.06    6CD    MD9<BR>1986   3.18    6PF    MD9<BR>1987   3.33    7CPC   MD9<BR>1987   2.84    7PSC   MD9<BR>1988   3.33    8CPC   MD9<BR>1988   2.84    8PSC   MD9<P><P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave Gunsul||04-26-2001||10:44 PM||||No, all V6 autos have either a 3.33 or 3.65<BR>whether they're SE's or GT's.<BR>85/86 V6 auto= 3.65 final drive <BR>87/88 V6 auto= 3.33 final drive <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000007||BC-GT||04-26-2001||11:08 PM||||rpo code  FW2   Transaxle, final drive, 3.06 ratio<BR>That's out of my 85 GT/V6 auto||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dave Gunsul||04-27-2001||05:16 PM||||I don't know what to tell ya, the book says<BR>3.65 for 85 V6. The way my stock 85 auto takes off and the higher RPM at 60 MPH<BR>Is definately different than my buddies stock<BR>87 GT. I also compared his 87 GT to my 86<BR>when stock and my 86 was still quicker off the line and RPMed higher at higher speeds.<BR>The obvious conclusion is that the 85/86 V6<BR>is a higher numerically geared auto trans.<P>Maybe you're looking at a different cars final drive ratio. Sometimes service manuals<BR>generalize the years. I have seen the same problem with Camaro rear end ratios.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
